## How Amazon SEO consulting works

Every engagement starts with a listing audit. I review your current listings, keyword targeting, content quality, images, A+ Content, and competitor positioning. You get a detailed report with prioritised recommendations.

From there, most clients choose one of two paths. Some want me to implement everything: I rewrite all listing copy, optimise backend terms, brief A+ Content, and monitor rankings over time. Others prefer to take the audit and recommendations back to their in-house team for implementation. I stay available for questions and review.

Either way I track keyword rankings and organic traffic after changes go live to measure the impact and iterate. Amazon SEO is not a one-and-done exercise: categories shift, competitors adjust, and Amazon regularly updates its algorithm. Ongoing optimisation keeps you ahead.

This fits within my broader [SEO consulting](/services/seo-consulting/) approach: data-driven, transparent, and focused on measurable commercial outcomes.

## Amazon SEO questions

### Is an Amazon listing audit worth it compared with other spend?

Yes when your listings are weak. No when the problem is price, stock or review count. The audit checks keyword gaps, indexing, titles, bullets, images and A+ content on your top 5 ASINs. A fixed £495 audit is a one-off cost where PPC is a running cost. Listing copy will not fix a price, stock or review problem on listings that already cover the basics. I will say so. The free 20-minute diagnosis tells you which case you are in. I do not promise a ranking or sales result.

### What happens to reviews when SKU changes create new ASINs?

Reviews belong to the ASIN. A new ASIN starts without them. In the audit I check three things. First, whether the old and new listings can be linked as variations, or merged where Amazon allows it for your category. Second, whether the new listing keeps the keyword coverage of the old one. Third, whether the old listing is still live, suppressed or competing with the new one. What Amazon permits depends on your category and account. I confirm the options after seeing the listings.

### Do you rewrite the listings or do I?

Either. Some clients have me rewrite all listing copy, backend terms and A+ briefs. Others take the audit and recommendations back to their in-house team. I stay available for questions.

